# File upload

Let users choose a local file when the task genuinely needs one.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for a dashboard image or a supported import file. Explain accepted formats and limits before selection. Keep the native file chooser available even if drag and drop is added.

## When not to use it

Do not require a file when the same task can be completed with existing data. A themed chooser must not be mistaken for a new backup or restore implementation.

## Home Assistant adaptation

The reference examples select files locally and do not send them anywhere. A production importer must validate file content, report progress and explain whether an import will replace settings before committing it. File selection is not proof that an upload or restore succeeded.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Provide a visible label and associate format guidance and errors. Do not make dragging the only interaction. Report the selected filename and allow replacement; browsers intentionally prevent prepopulating a file input after a failed request.

